	"WiFi 7: The Next Generation of Wireless Networking",
	"Everything you need to know about WiFi 7 (802.11be): speed improvements, MLO technology, 320MHz channels, and how it compares to WiFi 6E for home and business.",
	"<h1>WiFi 7: The Next Generation of Wireless Networking</h1>\n    <p>WiFi 7, also known as IEEE 802.11be, is the latest generation of wireless networking technology. Building on the foundations of WiFi 6 and WiFi 6E, WiFi 7 introduces groundbreaking features that dramatically increase speed, reduce latency, and improve reliability for all connected devices.</p>\n\n    <h2>Incredible Speed Improvements</h2>\n    <p>WiFi 7 offers theoretical maximum speeds of over 40 Gbps, nearly five times faster than WiFi 6 and twice as fast as WiFi 6E. This is achieved through several technologies: 320 MHz channel width (double WiFi 6's 160 MHz), 4096-QAM modulation (up from 1024-QAM), and multi-link operation (MLO) that aggregates multiple frequency bands simultaneously.</p>\n\n    <h2>Multi-Link Operation (MLO)</h2>\n    <p>MLO is the most significant innovation in WiFi 7. It allows devices to connect to multiple bands (2.4 GHz, 5 GHz, and 6 GHz) simultaneously, combining their bandwidth and using them as a single virtual link. This provides higher throughput, lower latency, and automatic failover if one band experiences interference. For real-time applications like video calls and gaming, MLO is transformative.</p>\n\n    <h2>Lower Latency for Real-Time Applications</h2>\n    <p>WiFi 7 introduces technologies specifically designed to reduce latency. Restricted Target Wake Time (R-TWT) schedules transmissions more efficiently, reducing contention. Multi-user MIMO improvements allow more simultaneous connections without degradation. These features make WiFi 7 ideal for cloud gaming, VR/AR applications, and real-time collaboration tools.</p>\n\n    <h2>WiFi 7 vs WiFi 6E: Should You Upgrade?</h2>\n    <p>WiFi 6E already brought the 6 GHz band to consumers, offering clean spectrum and high speeds. WiFi 7 builds on this with wider channels, MLO, and improved efficiency. For most users, WiFi 6E remains excellent for current needs. WiFi 7 becomes worthwhile for power users with gigabit internet connections, large file transfers, or demanding real-time applications.</p>\n\n    <h2>WiFi 7 Routers and Devices</h2>\n    <p>Major router manufacturers including TP-Link, Asus, Netgear, and Eero have released WiFi 7 routers. Prices range from $200 for basic models to $1,000+ for premium mesh systems. The latest flagship smartphones and laptops include WiFi 7 support, and the ecosystem will continue to expand as the standard becomes more widespread.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"footer\">\n        <p>WiFi 7 represents a significant leap forward in wireless networking technology. As more devices support the standard and router prices decrease, WiFi 7 will become the new normal for high-performance home and business networks.</p>\n        <p style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:0.85em;opacity:0.7;\">📊 <span id=\"busuanzi_container_site_pv\">Total visits <span id=\"busuanzi_value_site_pv\"></span></span><span id=\"visitor-ip\"></span></p>\n    </div>\n    <script>fetch('https://api.ipify.org?format=json').then(r=>r.json()).then(d=>{var el=document.getElementById('visitor-ip');if(el&&d.ip){var ips=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('ip_list')||'[]');if(!ips.includes(d.ip)){ips.push(d.ip);localStorage.setItem('ip_list',JSON.stringify(ips))}el.innerHTML=' | 🖥️ Your IP: '+d.ip+' | Unique IPs: '+ips.length}}).catch(function(){})<\/script>\n    <div id=\"like-box\"></div>\n    <div id=\"related-articles\"></div>",
	"src/content/dev-tools/articles/tech-16.md",
