	"<h1>WiFi 7: The Next Generation of Wireless Networking</h1>\n    <p>WiFi 7, also known as IEEE 802.11be, is the latest generation of wireless networking technology. Building on the foundations of WiFi 6 and WiFi 6E, WiFi 7 introduces groundbreaking features that dramatically increase speed, reduce latency, and improve reliability for all connected devices.</p>\n<pre class=\"astro-code github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8; overflow-x: auto;\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"plaintext\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;h2&gt;Incredible Speed Improvements&lt;/h2&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p&gt;WiFi 7 offers theoretical maximum speeds of over 40 Gbps, nearly five times faster than WiFi 6 and twice as fast as WiFi 6E. This is achieved through several technologies: 320 MHz channel width (double WiFi 6's 160 MHz), 4096-QAM modulation (up from 1024-QAM), and multi-link operation (MLO) that aggregates multiple frequency bands simultaneously.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;h2&gt;Multi-Link Operation (MLO)&lt;/h2&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p&gt;MLO is the most significant innovation in WiFi 7. It allows devices to connect to multiple bands (2.4 GHz, 5 GHz, and 6 GHz) simultaneously, combining their bandwidth and using them as a single virtual link. This provides higher throughput, lower latency, and automatic failover if one band experiences interference. For real-time applications like video calls and gaming, MLO is transformative.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;h2&gt;Lower Latency for Real-Time Applications&lt;/h2&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p&gt;WiFi 7 introduces technologies specifically designed to reduce latency. Restricted Target Wake Time (R-TWT) schedules transmissions more efficiently, reducing contention. Multi-user MIMO improvements allow more simultaneous connections without degradation. These features make WiFi 7 ideal for cloud gaming, VR/AR applications, and real-time collaboration tools.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;h2&gt;WiFi 7 vs WiFi 6E: Should You Upgrade?&lt;/h2&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p&gt;WiFi 6E already brought the 6 GHz band to consumers, offering clean spectrum and high speeds. WiFi 7 builds on this with wider channels, MLO, and improved efficiency. For most users, WiFi 6E remains excellent for current needs. WiFi 7 becomes worthwhile for power users with gigabit internet connections, large file transfers, or demanding real-time applications.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;h2&gt;WiFi 7 Routers and Devices&lt;/h2&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p&gt;Major router manufacturers including TP-Link, Asus, Netgear, and Eero have released WiFi 7 routers. Prices range from $200 for basic models to $1,000+ for premium mesh systems. The latest flagship smartphones and laptops include WiFi 7 support, and the ecosystem will continue to expand as the standard becomes more widespread.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;div class=\"footer\"&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;p&gt;WiFi 7 represents a significant leap forward in wireless networking technology. As more devices support the standard and router prices decrease, WiFi 7 will become the new normal for high-performance home and business networks.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;p style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:0.85em;opacity:0.7;\"&gt;📊 &lt;span id=\"busuanzi_container_site_pv\"&gt;Total visits &lt;span id=\"busuanzi_value_site_pv\"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span id=\"visitor-ip\"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;/div&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;script&gt;fetch('https://api.ipify.org?format=json').then(r=&gt;r.json()).then(d=&gt;{var el=document.getElementById('visitor-ip');if(el&amp;&amp;d.ip){var ips=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('ip_list')||'[]');if(!ips.includes(d.ip)){ips.push(d.ip);localStorage.setItem('ip_list',JSON.stringify(ips))}el.innerHTML=' | 🖥️ Your IP: '+d.ip+' | Unique IPs: '+ips.length}}).catch(function(){})&lt;/script&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;div id=\"like-box\"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;div id=\"related-articles\"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</span></span></code></pre>\n",
