	"AWS Guide: Amazon Web Services Explained",
	"A comprehensive guide to Amazon Web Services: core services like EC2, S3, Lambda, pricing models, common use cases, and how AWS dominates cloud computing.",
	"<h1>AWS Guide: Amazon Web Services Explained</h1>\n    <p>Amazon Web Services (AWS) is the world's leading cloud computing platform, offering over 200 services across computing, storage, databases, machine learning, analytics, and more. Since its launch in 2006, AWS has transformed how organizations build and deploy applications, enabling unprecedented scalability and flexibility.</p>\n\n    <h2>Core Compute Services: EC2 and Lambda</h2>\n    <p>Amazon EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) provides virtual servers in the cloud, offering complete control over the computing environment. You can choose from a vast array of instance types optimized for different workloads. AWS Lambda offers serverless computing, where you upload code and AWS runs it in response to events without provisioning or managing servers. Lambda scales automatically and you pay only for the compute time consumed.</p>\n\n    <h2>Storage Services: S3 and EBS</h2>\n    <p>Amazon S3 (Simple Storage Service) is object storage designed for any amount of data. It offers 99.999999999% durability and is used for backups, data lakes, static website hosting, and content distribution. Amazon EBS (Elastic Block Store) provides persistent block storage for EC2 instances, similar to virtual hard drives. S3 and EBS form the foundation of data storage on AWS.</p>\n\n    <h2>Database Services</h2>\n    <p>AWS offers a wide range of database services: Amazon RDS for relational databases (MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQL Server, Oracle); Amazon DynamoDB for NoSQL key-value and document databases; Amazon Aurora for high-performance MySQL/PostgreSQL-compatible databases; and Amazon Redshift for data warehousing. Each service is fully managed, handling backups, patching, and replication automatically.</p>\n\n    <h2>AWS Pricing Model</h2>\n    <p>AWS follows a pay-as-you-go pricing model, charging for compute hours, storage consumed, and data transferred. The AWS Free Tier allows new customers to explore many services free for 12 months. Pricing can be optimized through Reserved Instances (committing to 1 or 3 years for discounts), Spot Instances (using spare capacity at up to 90% discount), and Savings Plans (flexible pricing based on commitment).</p>\n\n    <h2>Common Use Cases</h2>\n    <p>AWS powers a vast range of applications: hosting websites and web applications, running enterprise applications, storing and analyzing big data, training and deploying machine learning models, delivering content via CloudFront CDN, running backup and disaster recovery, and supporting IoT device connectivity. Most of the internet's most popular services run on AWS infrastructure.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"footer\">\n        <p>AWS continues to dominate the cloud computing market with its comprehensive service portfolio, global infrastructure spanning over 30 regions, and continuous innovation. Whether you are a startup or enterprise, AWS provides the tools to build virtually any application at scale.</p>\n        <p style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:0.85em;opacity:0.7;\">📊 <span id=\"busuanzi_container_site_pv\">Total visits <span id=\"busuanzi_value_site_pv\"></span></span><span id=\"visitor-ip\"></span></p>\n    </div>\n    <script>fetch('https://api.ipify.org?format=json').then(r=>r.json()).then(d=>{var el=document.getElementById('visitor-ip');if(el&&d.ip){var ips=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('ip_list')||'[]');if(!ips.includes(d.ip)){ips.push(d.ip);localStorage.setItem('ip_list',JSON.stringify(ips))}el.innerHTML=' | 🖥️ Your IP: '+d.ip+' | Unique IPs: '+ips.length}}).catch(function(){})<\/script>\n    <div id=\"like-box\"></div>\n    <div id=\"related-articles\"></div>",
