	"Python Programming Guide for Beginners",
	"A beginner's guide to Python programming: why Python is popular, basic concepts, popular frameworks, career paths, and how to start learning Python in 2026.",
	"<h1>Python Programming Guide for Beginners</h1>\n    <p>Python is one of the most popular and versatile programming languages in the world. Known for its readable syntax and extensive ecosystem, Python is used in web development, data science, artificial intelligence, automation, scientific computing, and more. It is widely regarded as the best language for beginners to learn programming.</p>\n\n    <h2>Why Python Is So Popular</h2>\n    <p>Python's popularity stems from its clean, readable syntax that emphasizes natural language. The language follows a batteries-included philosophy with a comprehensive standard library. Python has a massive ecosystem of third-party packages available through pip (Python's package manager). It supports multiple programming paradigms including procedural, object-oriented, and functional programming.</p>\n\n    <h2>Python Fundamentals</h2>\n    <p>Key Python concepts include variables and data types (integers, floats, strings, lists, dictionaries, tuples), control flow (if/else, for loops, while loops), functions and modules, file I/O, exception handling, and classes. Python's dynamic typing and interpreted nature make it easy to experiment and iterate quickly. Understanding these fundamentals provides a solid foundation for any programming career.</p>\n\n    <h2>Popular Frameworks and Libraries</h2>\n    <p>Python's ecosystem includes powerful frameworks for every domain: Django and Flask for web development; Pandas, NumPy, and Matplotlib for data analysis and visualization; TensorFlow, PyTorch, and scikit-learn for machine learning; FastAPI for building APIs; Selenium and Playwright for automation; and Pygame for game development. The package index (PyPI) hosts over 500,000 projects.</p>\n\n    <h2>Python in AI and Data Science</h2>\n    <p>Python has become the de facto language for artificial intelligence and data science. Libraries like NumPy provide numerical computing foundations; Pandas offers data manipulation tools; Matplotlib and Seaborn handle visualization; and scikit-learn, TensorFlow, and PyTorch provide machine learning capabilities. Jupyter notebooks offer an interactive development environment popular among data scientists.</p>\n\n    <h2>Getting Started with Python</h2>\n    <p>To start learning Python, install Python 3.12+ from python.org, choose an IDE (VS Code with Python extension, PyCharm, or Thonny for beginners), and start with online resources like the official Python tutorial, Codecademy, or freeCodeCamp. Practice regularly by building small projects, contribute to open source, and join Python communities for support and learning opportunities.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"footer\">\n        <p>Python's combination of simplicity and power makes it an ideal first programming language and a valuable tool for experienced developers. Its versatility across domains ensures that Python skills remain in high demand across the technology industry.</p>\n        <p style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:0.85em;opacity:0.7;\">📊 <span id=\"busuanzi_container_site_pv\">Total visits <span id=\"busuanzi_value_site_pv\"></span></span><span id=\"visitor-ip\"></span></p>\n    </div>\n    <script>fetch('https://api.ipify.org?format=json').then(r=>r.json()).then(d=>{var el=document.getElementById('visitor-ip');if(el&&d.ip){var ips=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('ip_list')||'[]');if(!ips.includes(d.ip)){ips.push(d.ip);localStorage.setItem('ip_list',JSON.stringify(ips))}el.innerHTML=' | 🖥️ Your IP: '+d.ip+' | Unique IPs: '+ips.length}}).catch(function(){})<\/script>\n    <div id=\"like-box\"></div>\n    <div id=\"related-articles\"></div>",
