	"JavaScript Essentials: A Complete Guide",
	"A complete guide to JavaScript: ES6+ features, the DOM, async programming, popular frameworks like React and Node.js, and modern JavaScript development practices.",
	"<h1>JavaScript Essentials: A Complete Guide</h1>\n    <p>JavaScript is the programming language of the web, powering interactive websites and web applications. It has evolved dramatically from its early days as a simple scripting language into a versatile, high-performance language used for frontend, backend, mobile, and desktop development.</p>\n\n    <h2>Modern JavaScript (ES6+)</h2>\n    <p>ECMAScript 2015 (ES6) introduced major improvements to JavaScript: arrow functions provide concise syntax; let and const replace var for better scoping; template literals simplify string interpolation; destructuring extracts values from objects and arrays; spread and rest operators handle collections elegantly; classes provide syntactic sugar for prototypal inheritance; and modules enable code organization.</p>\n\n    <h2>The DOM and Browser APIs</h2>\n    <p>The Document Object Model (DOM) represents HTML documents as a tree structure that JavaScript can manipulate. Key DOM operations include selecting elements, modifying content and styles, handling events, and creating animations. Browser APIs extend JavaScript's capabilities: Fetch API for network requests, LocalStorage for client-side data, Geolocation API, Canvas for graphics, and WebSockets for real-time communication.</p>\n\n    <h2>Async JavaScript: Promises and Async/Await</h2>\n    <p>JavaScript handles asynchronous operations through callbacks, Promises, and async/await. Promises represent eventual completion of asynchronous operations, avoiding callback hell. The async/await syntax (introduced in ES2017) makes asynchronous code read like synchronous code, greatly improving readability and error handling. Understanding the event loop and microtask queue is essential for mastering async JavaScript.</p>\n\n    <h2>Frontend Frameworks: React, Vue, and Angular</h2>\n    <p>React, developed by Meta, uses a component-based architecture with a virtual DOM for efficient rendering. Vue offers a progressive framework that is easy to learn and integrate. Angular, maintained by Google, is a comprehensive framework with built-in tools for large-scale applications. All three frameworks support modern development practices like hooks, reactive state management, and server-side rendering.</p>\n\n    <h2>Node.js and Server-Side JavaScript</h2>\n    <p>Node.js allows JavaScript to run on servers, enabling full-stack development with a single language. Its event-driven, non-blocking I/O model makes it efficient for handling concurrent connections. The npm ecosystem is the largest package registry in the world. Express.js is the most popular web framework, while Next.js and Nuxt provide full-stack frameworks with server-side rendering capabilities.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"footer\">\n        <p>JavaScript's versatility and universal browser support make it an essential skill for web developers. Whether you are building interactive frontends, scalable backends, or mobile apps, JavaScript provides the tools and ecosystem you need.</p>\n        <p style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:0.85em;opacity:0.7;\">📊 <span id=\"busuanzi_container_site_pv\">Total visits <span id=\"busuanzi_value_site_pv\"></span></span><span id=\"visitor-ip\"></span></p>\n    </div>\n    <script>fetch('https://api.ipify.org?format=json').then(r=>r.json()).then(d=>{var el=document.getElementById('visitor-ip');if(el&&d.ip){var ips=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('ip_list')||'[]');if(!ips.includes(d.ip)){ips.push(d.ip);localStorage.setItem('ip_list',JSON.stringify(ips))}el.innerHTML=' | 🖥️ Your IP: '+d.ip+' | Unique IPs: '+ips.length}}).catch(function(){})<\/script>\n    <div id=\"like-box\"></div>\n    <div id=\"related-articles\"></div>",
	"src/content/dev-tools/guides/tech-32.md",
