	"Web Development Basics: HTML, CSS, and Beyond",
	"A beginner-friendly guide to web development: HTML structure, CSS styling, responsive design, accessibility basics, and the tools you need to build modern websites.",
	"<h1>Web Development Basics: HTML, CSS, and Beyond</h1>\n    <p>Web development is the process of building websites and web applications. It encompasses everything from simple static pages to complex interactive platforms. Understanding the fundamentals of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript is the first step on the journey to becoming a web developer.</p>\n\n    <h2>HTML: The Structure of the Web</h2>\n    <p>HyperText Markup Language (HTML) provides the structure and content of web pages. HTML uses elements (tags) to define headings, paragraphs, links, images, lists, tables, and forms. Semantic HTML uses meaningful elements like header, nav, main, article, section, and footer to describe content structure, improving accessibility and search engine optimization.</p>\n\n    <h2>CSS: Styling and Layout</h2>\n    <p>Cascading Style Sheets (CSS) controls the visual presentation of HTML elements. CSS handles colors, fonts, spacing, positioning, and responsive layouts. Modern CSS includes powerful layout systems: Flexbox for one-dimensional layouts and CSS Grid for two-dimensional layouts. CSS animations and transitions add interactivity without JavaScript. CSS custom properties (variables) enable maintainable, themeable stylesheets.</p>\n\n    <h2>Responsive Web Design</h2>\n    <p>Responsive design ensures websites look and function well on all devices, from phones to desktops. Key techniques include fluid grids using relative units (%, rem, vw/vh), flexible images with max-width: 100%, and media queries that apply different styles based on screen size. Mobile-first design starts with the smallest screen and progressively enhances for larger screens.</p>\n\n    <h2>Web Accessibility (A11Y)</h2>\n    <p>Web accessibility ensures that websites are usable by people with disabilities. Key practices include using semantic HTML, providing alt text for images, ensuring sufficient color contrast, supporting keyboard navigation, using ARIA attributes when necessary, and testing with screen readers. Accessibility benefits all users and is increasingly required by legal regulations worldwide.</p>\n\n    <h2>Development Tools and Workflow</h2>\n    <p>Modern web development uses various tools: VS Code as the preferred code editor; browser DevTools for debugging and testing; Git for version control; npm for package management; and build tools like Vite or Webpack for optimizing code. Learning to use these tools effectively is as important as learning the languages themselves.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"footer\">\n        <p>Web development is a rewarding field that combines creativity with technical skills. Starting with solid HTML and CSS fundamentals provides the foundation for learning more advanced technologies like JavaScript frameworks, backend development, and full-stack engineering.</p>\n        <p style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:0.85em;opacity:0.7;\">📊 <span id=\"busuanzi_container_site_pv\">Total visits <span id=\"busuanzi_value_site_pv\"></span></span><span id=\"visitor-ip\"></span></p>\n    </div>\n    <script>fetch('https://api.ipify.org?format=json').then(r=>r.json()).then(d=>{var el=document.getElementById('visitor-ip');if(el&&d.ip){var ips=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('ip_list')||'[]');if(!ips.includes(d.ip)){ips.push(d.ip);localStorage.setItem('ip_list',JSON.stringify(ips))}el.innerHTML=' | 🖥️ Your IP: '+d.ip+' | Unique IPs: '+ips.length}}).catch(function(){})<\/script>\n    <div id=\"like-box\"></div>\n    <div id=\"related-articles\"></div>",
