	"Security Camera Guide: Home Surveillance 2026",
	"A guide to home security cameras in 2026: indoor vs outdoor, wired vs wireless, AI detection features, privacy considerations, and the best security camera systems.",
	"<h1>Security Camera Guide: Home Surveillance 2026</h1>\n    <p>Home security cameras have become sophisticated tools for protecting your property and loved ones. Modern cameras offer AI-powered detection, high-resolution video, night vision, two-way audio, and seamless integration with smart home systems. This guide covers everything you need to know about choosing and using security cameras.</p>\n\n    <h2>Indoor vs Outdoor Cameras</h2>\n    <p>Outdoor cameras must withstand weather conditions with IP65 or higher ratings for water and dust resistance. They typically have wider viewing angles and better night vision. Indoor cameras focus on compact design, privacy features (physical shutters), and often include pet monitoring and baby crying detection. Many cameras now offer AI differentiation between people, vehicles, animals, and packages.</p>\n\n    <h2>Wired vs Wireless: Pros and Cons</h2>\n    <p>Wired cameras provide reliable power and dedicated video transmission without WiFi congestion. They are ideal for continuous recording but require professional installation. Wireless cameras (battery-powered) offer flexible placement and easy DIY installation but require periodic battery charging and depend on WiFi signal strength. Some systems use Power over Ethernet (PoE) for both power and data through a single cable.</p>\n\n    <h2>Resolution and Night Vision</h2>\n    <p>1080p is the minimum standard, while 2K and 4K cameras provide significantly more detail for identifying faces and license plates. Night vision technologies include infrared (IR) for black-and-white night vision, color night vision using ambient light or built-in spotlights, and thermal imaging for detecting heat signatures. Wide dynamic range (WDR) helps handle challenging lighting conditions with bright and dark areas.</p>\n\n    <h2>AI and Smart Detection Features</h2>\n    <p>Modern cameras use AI for intelligent detection: person detection reduces false alarms from animals or moving leaves; vehicle detection monitors driveways; package detection alerts you to deliveries; facial recognition identifies known individuals; and anomaly detection learns normal activity patterns and flags unusual events. Local AI processing (on-camera) is preferred over cloud-based processing for privacy and lower latency.</p>\n\n    <h2>Privacy and Data Storage</h2>\n    <p>Security camera privacy has become a major concern. Consider where video is stored: local storage (microSD, NVR, HomeKit Secure Video) keeps footage on your property; cloud storage offers remote access but raises privacy questions. End-to-end encryption ensures only you can view footage. Features like privacy zones, scheduling, and physical shutters provide additional control over when and where cameras record.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"footer\">\n        <p>Home security cameras provide peace of mind and valuable evidence when incidents occur. Choose cameras with AI detection, local storage options, and strong privacy features. Consider your specific needs: outdoor coverage, package detection, or indoor monitoring, and select accordingly.</p>\n        <p style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:0.85em;opacity:0.7;\">📊 <span id=\"busuanzi_container_site_pv\">Total visits <span id=\"busuanzi_value_site_pv\"></span></span><span id=\"visitor-ip\"></span></p>\n    </div>\n    <script>fetch('https://api.ipify.org?format=json').then(r=>r.json()).then(d=>{var el=document.getElementById('visitor-ip');if(el&&d.ip){var ips=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('ip_list')||'[]');if(!ips.includes(d.ip)){ips.push(d.ip);localStorage.setItem('ip_list',JSON.stringify(ips))}el.innerHTML=' | 🖥️ Your IP: '+d.ip+' | Unique IPs: '+ips.length}}).catch(function(){})<\/script>\n    <div id=\"like-box\"></div>\n    <div id=\"related-articles\"></div>",
	"src/content/tech-products/guides/tech-39.md",
