	"Blockchain Technology Beyond Cryptocurrency",
	"An exploration of blockchain technology applications beyond cryptocurrency: supply chain, healthcare, digital identity, smart contracts, and decentralized finance (DeFi).",
	"<h1>Blockchain Technology Beyond Cryptocurrency</h1>\n    <p>Blockchain is a distributed ledger technology that enables secure, transparent, and tamper-proof record-keeping without a central authority. While most people associate blockchain with cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin, the technology has far broader applications across industries, offering solutions to problems of trust, transparency, and efficiency.</p>\n\n    <h2>How Blockchain Works</h2>\n    <p>A blockchain is a chain of blocks, each containing a batch of transactions or data. Each block references the previous block through a cryptographic hash, creating an immutable chain. The ledger is distributed across a network of computers (nodes), and consensus mechanisms like proof-of-work or proof-of-stake ensure agreement on the state of the ledger. This design makes it extremely difficult to alter historical data without network consensus.</p>\n\n    <h2>Smart Contracts</h2>\n    <p>Smart contracts are self-executing contracts with terms directly written into code. They automatically execute when predetermined conditions are met, without requiring intermediaries. Ethereum popularized smart contracts, and they are now used for decentralized finance (DeFi), insurance claims, supply chain automation, and digital rights management. Smart contracts reduce administrative costs and eliminate the need for trust between parties.</p>\n\n    <h2>Supply Chain Transparency</h2>\n    <p>Blockchain provides end-to-end visibility in supply chains, recording every step of a product's journey from raw materials to consumer. This enables verification of ethical sourcing, authenticity of luxury goods, food safety tracking (quickly identifying contamination sources), and compliance with regulations. Major companies including Walmart, IBM, and Maersk have implemented blockchain supply chain solutions.</p>\n\n    <h2>Digital Identity and Credentials</h2>\n    <p>Blockchain-based digital identity systems give individuals control over their personal data. Instead of relying on centralized identity providers, users can store verified credentials on a blockchain and share them selectively. Applications include self-sovereign identity (SSI), verifiable credentials for education and professional qualifications, and secure digital voting systems that ensure transparency while protecting voter privacy.</p>\n\n    <h2>Challenges and Limitations</h2>\n    <p>Blockchain technology faces several challenges: scalability (many blockchains process fewer transactions per second than traditional databases); energy consumption (proof-of-work systems like Bitcoin); regulatory uncertainty; interoperability between different blockchain networks; and the complexity of implementation. Layer 2 solutions, proof-of-stake consensus, and sharding are being developed to address scalability and energy concerns.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"footer\">\n        <p>Blockchain technology has evolved beyond its cryptocurrency origins to offer solutions for transparency, security, and efficiency across industries. While challenges remain, the technology continues to mature and find practical applications in supply chain, identity, finance, and governance.</p>\n        <p style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:0.85em;opacity:0.7;\">📊 <span id=\"busuanzi_container_site_pv\">Total visits <span id=\"busuanzi_value_site_pv\"></span></span><span id=\"visitor-ip\"></span></p>\n    </div>\n    <script>fetch('https://api.ipify.org?format=json').then(r=>r.json()).then(d=>{var el=document.getElementById('visitor-ip');if(el&&d.ip){var ips=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('ip_list')||'[]');if(!ips.includes(d.ip)){ips.push(d.ip);localStorage.setItem('ip_list',JSON.stringify(ips))}el.innerHTML=' | 🖥️ Your IP: '+d.ip+' | Unique IPs: '+ips.length}}).catch(function(){})<\/script>\n    <div id=\"like-box\"></div>\n    <div id=\"related-articles\"></div>",
