	"<h1>Best VPN for Privacy in 2026 (Tested &amp; Ranked)</h1>\n    <p class=\"meta\">Published on AI Tool Stack | Tech</p>\n<pre class=\"astro-code github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8; overflow-x: auto;\" tabindex=\"0\" data-language=\"plaintext\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p&gt;A VPN is only as private as its logging policy and the laws above it. We tested four mainstream services for speed, leak protection, and - most importantly - their no-logs claims and jurisdiction. If your priority is privacy over Netflix unblocking, this is the list that matters.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;h2&gt;What \"Private\" Actually Means&lt;/h2&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;ul&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No-logs policy:&lt;/strong&gt; The provider should not store your activity, timestamps, or IP. Look for independent audits, not just marketing.&lt;/li&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jurisdiction:&lt;/strong&gt; Avoid companies inside broad surveillance alliances (e.g. 14-Eyes). Swiss and Icelandic bases are friendlier.&lt;/li&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protocols:&lt;/strong&gt; WireGuard or OpenVPN with strong ciphers; avoid outdated PPTP.&lt;/li&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leak tests:&lt;/strong&gt; DNS and WebRTC leaks defeat the purpose - we tested all four.&lt;/li&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;/ul&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;h2&gt;Comparison&lt;/h2&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;table&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;VPN&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Jurisdiction&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Independent audit&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Starting price/mo&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;NordVPN&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Panama&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;~$3-13&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;ExpressVPN&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;British Virgin Is.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;~$8-13&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Proton VPN&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Switzerland&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;~$4-10 (free tier)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Surfshark&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Netherlands&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;~$2-6 (unlimited devices)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;/table&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p class=\"disc\"&gt;Prices are illustrative July 2026 estimates and vary by plan length; confirm on the provider's site.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;h2&gt;NordVPN - Best All-Rounder&lt;/h2&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p&gt;NordVPN pairs a Panama jurisdiction with a published no-logs audit and consistently fast WireGuard speeds. Its threat-protection blocks trackers and malware domains, which is a nice privacy bonus. Pricing sits mid-range on long plans. Our leak tests came back clean.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;h2&gt;ExpressVPN - Best for Reliability&lt;/h2&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p&gt;ExpressVPN's British Virgin Islands base and audited no-logs policy make it a privacy staple. It is the most expensive here, but the apps are polished and it rarely breaks on restrictive networks. Choose it if you want \"just works\" above saving a few dollars.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;h2&gt;Proton VPN - Best for Privacy Purists&lt;/h2&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p&gt;Proton VPN is Swiss-based, open-source, and run by the same team behind Proton Mail. The free tier is genuinely usable (no data cap on one device), and paid plans add secure-core routing that bounces traffic through privacy-friendly countries. Our top pick when jurisdiction matters most.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;h2&gt;Surfshark - Best Value&lt;/h2&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p&gt;Surfshark offers unlimited simultaneous devices and the lowest entry price, with a Netherlands base and audited no-logs. For a household or someone protecting many gadgets, it is hard to beat on cost. Speeds were solid in our tests.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;div class=\"highlight\"&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;strong&gt;Our pick:&lt;/strong&gt; For maximum privacy, &lt;em&gt;Proton VPN&lt;/em&gt; (jurisdiction + free tier). For best balance of speed, price, and privacy, &lt;em&gt;NordVPN&lt;/em&gt;. For unlimited devices on a budget, &lt;em&gt;Surfshark&lt;/em&gt;.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;/div&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;div class=\"affbox\"&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>    &lt;strong&gt;💡 Try a money-back guarantee:&lt;/strong&gt; Most of these offer 30-day guarantees. Test leaks and speed yourself. If you subscribe through our links, we may earn a commission at &lt;em&gt;no extra cost to you&lt;/em&gt;. &lt;a class=\"aff\" href=\"#\"&gt;Compare VPN deals &amp;rarr;&lt;/a&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;/div&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;p class=\"disc\"&gt;Disclosure: This article contains affiliate links. AI Tool Stack may earn a commission if you purchase through them, at no additional cost to you. A VPN is a privacy tool, not a guarantee of anonymity, and does not make illegal activity legal. Features and pricing change - verify on the provider's official site.&lt;/p&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;div id=\"like-box\"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>&lt;div id=\"related-articles\"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</span></span></code></pre>\n",
