	"Windows 12: What to Expect",
	"An overview of Windows 12 features, system requirements, release timeline, and what Microsoft's next-generation operating system brings to users.",
	"<h1>Windows 12: What to Expect</h1>\n    <p>Microsoft's next major operating system release promises to build upon Windows 11 with deeper AI integration, a refreshed user interface, and improved performance. Windows 12 represents a significant step forward in Microsoft's vision for modern computing.</p>\n\n    <h2>AI-Powered Features</h2>\n    <p>Windows 12 is expected to integrate AI deeply into the operating system. This includes a more advanced Copilot assistant that can control system settings, suggest workflows, and automate repetitive tasks. AI-powered search will understand natural language queries and find files based on content and context rather than just file names.</p>\n\n    <h2>Redesigned User Interface</h2>\n    <p>The Windows 12 desktop is rumored to feature a floating taskbar, redesigned system tray, and more customizable widgets. The Start menu may see further refinements with better organization and Live Tiles making a potential return in a modernized form. The overall aesthetic is expected to be cleaner and more cohesive.</p>\n\n    <h2>System Requirements</h2>\n    <p>Windows 12 will likely require similar hardware to Windows 11, including TPM 2.0 and Secure Boot support. However, AI features may demand more capable hardware, including NPUs (Neural Processing Units) for local AI processing. Microsoft is expected to phase out support for older processors without certain instruction set extensions.</p>\n\n    <h2>Performance and Security Improvements</h2>\n    <p>Under the hood, Windows 12 will bring optimizations for modern hybrid CPU architectures, better memory management, and improved battery life for laptops. Security enhancements include stronger default encryption, improved credential guard, and better protection against firmware-level attacks.</p>\n\n    <h2>Cloud Integration</h2>\n    <p>Windows 12 will likely deepen integration with Microsoft 365 and Azure cloud services. Features like Windows 365 Boot could make cloud PCs more seamless, and OneDrive integration will become more sophisticated with better file-on-demand and backup capabilities.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"footer\">\n        <p>Windows 12 is shaping up to be a thoughtful evolution of the platform, with AI at its core. Existing Windows 11 users should expect a smooth transition, while the new AI features may finally give compelling reasons for Windows 10 holdouts to upgrade.</p>\n        <p style=\"margin-top:12px;font-size:0.85em;opacity:0.7;\">📊 <span id=\"busuanzi_container_site_pv\">Total visits <span id=\"busuanzi_value_site_pv\"></span></span><span id=\"visitor-ip\"></span></p>\n    </div>\n    <script>fetch('https://api.ipify.org?format=json').then(r=>r.json()).then(d=>{var el=document.getElementById('visitor-ip');if(el&&d.ip){var ips=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('ip_list')||'[]');if(!ips.includes(d.ip)){ips.push(d.ip);localStorage.setItem('ip_list',JSON.stringify(ips))}el.innerHTML=' | 🖥️ Your IP: '+d.ip+' | Unique IPs: '+ips.length}}).catch(function(){})<\/script>\n    <div id=\"like-box\"></div>\n    <div id=\"related-articles\"></div>",
